* Super-lead preamp, stage 3 of 4: the mixing node, V3b and V3a (the cathode follower). V1a's plate (stage 1) arrives through VL2 and V2b's plate
* (stage 2) through VL3. The FX divider and V4b's grid network are repeated here as V3a's load. See preamp.net for how the netlist is split.

.nodes x p1a c7n x1 g3b p2b ww p3b k3b kcf sj g4b

V VRAIL x 314.8 378

S VL2 p1a 1 0
S VL3 p2b 1 0
C C7 p1a c7n 0.02u
R R17 c7n x1 2M2
C C8 c7n x1 120p
R R18 x1 0 330k
R R21 x1 g3b 220k
C C10 p2b ww 0.02u
R R20 ww 0 2M2
R OPT2 ww x1 1G

T V3B g3b p3b k3b 12AX7
R R22 x p3b 220k
R R23 k3b 0 1k8
C C11 k3b 0 1u
T V3A p3b x kcf 12AX7
R R25 kcf sj 100k
R R24 sj 0 2k2
C C12 sj g4b 1u
R R26 g4b 0 1M
